Here's a Slash'em question.  I am playing a vampiric barbarian and have
just reached the sunless sea.  Now it seems to me that I have no way of
retrieving the magic lamp in the sea.  The standard approach is to
detect it (blessed magic mapping or object detection) go there, freeze
the sea, dig a pit and take it.

Because vampires are flying, they cannot pick up things from a pit
(except on the first Sokoban level, maybe).  Typical solutions in the
normal dungeon are to either dig through the pit and get the desired
item on the level beneath (but find it first) or teleport the item out
of the pit (same proviso).  The first solution will not work on a single
branching level such as the sunless sea, the second might teleport the
lamp to another water square (this I am not sure about), which would
make things very tedious, as I might end up freezing the whole level.
(I do not have enough wands of cold for that.)

With polymorph control and / of polymorph, I might turn into a
non-flying creature to get the lamp, but I don't have polycontrol.

Any other ideas?
